§ `s 2 -- Am I an applicable person`

#ASSERT NOT `Am I an applicable person` `a foreigner aged 40 with the same balances`
#ASSERT `Am I an applicable person` `a foreigner aged 40 of a prescribed class`

§ `s 15(2) -- On what ground may I withdraw`

#ASSERT `On what ground may I withdraw` `a citizen aged 60 with $200,000, $60,000 of it medisave` EQUALS `section 15(2)(a): I have attained 55`
#ASSERT `On what ground may I withdraw` `a foreigner aged 40 with the same balances` EQUALS `section 15(2)(b): I am not an applicable person`

§ `ss 15(6) and 16(1) -- How much may I withdraw`

#ASSERT `How much may I withdraw, once the Board authorises it` `a citizen aged 60 with $200,000, $60,000 of it medisave` EQUALS 40000
#ASSERT `How much may I withdraw, once the Board authorises it` `a foreigner aged 40 with the same balances` EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `How much may I withdraw, once the Board authorises it` `a citizen aged 60 whose medisave is $150,000` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much may I withdraw, once the Board authorises it` `a citizen aged 60 with a $20,000 reserved amount` EQUALS 20000

§ `s 15(1)`

#ASSERT `May money be paid out to me now` `a citizen aged 60 with $200,000, $60,000 of it medisave`
#ASSERT NOT `May money be paid out to me now` `a citizen aged 60 still awaiting the Board's authority`

§ `s 15(3)`

#ASSERT `Am I entitled to a further withdrawal under section 15(3)` `a citizen aged 56 who withdrew at 55, with a birthday since`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I entitled to a further withdrawal under section 15(3)` `a foreigner aged 40 with the same balances`

§ `s 24(2)`

#ASSERT NOT `Can my CPF money be taken for my debts or in my bankruptcy` FALSE

§ `ss 24(3A), 24(3B), 25(5) -- Where does my CPF money go when I die`

#ASSERT `Where does my CPF money go when I die` `a nomination still standing` EQUALS `held on trust for my nominees, outside my estate and free of my debts`
#ASSERT `Where does my CPF money go when I die` `a nomination made before I married` EQUALS `held on trust for those entitled through the Public Trustee under section 25A, outside my estate and free of my debts`
#ASSERT `Where does my CPF money go when I die` `money payable to my former spouse under section 27B` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: section 24(3A) does not apply to money payable under section 27B`

§ `s 25(1) -- May I make a nomination`

#ASSERT `May I make a nomination` `a citizen aged 16`
#ASSERT NOT `May I make a nomination` `a citizen aged 15`
#ASSERT NOT `May I make a nomination` `a foreigner aged 40 with the same balances`

§ `s 25(1)(a) and 25(3) -- how my nominee receives it`

#ASSERT `How much of the portion goes into my nominee's own CPF accounts` `my son, 30, a citizen, $300,000 by transfer, with a $200,000 Ministerial maximum` EQUALS 200000
#ASSERT `How much of the portion goes into my nominee's own CPF accounts` `my son, 30, a citizen, $300,000 by payment` EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `Is my nominee's money paid to the Public Trustee instead` `my daughter, 12, $50,000 by payment`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my nominee's money paid to the Public Trustee instead` `my widow, 17, $50,000 by payment`

